            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital admission of your patient, an 80-year-old male, admitted on 14/04/2012 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, physical examination revealed reduced air entry bilaterally with expiratory wheeze. Oxygen saturation was diminished on pulse oximetry. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed type 2 respiratory failure. Chest X-ray excluded pneumothorax or consolidation. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, controlled oxygen therapy, and received intravenous fluids for hydration. He responded well to treatment with improvement in respiratory function. He is discharged in stable condition with optimised inhaler regimen and oral steroids taper. Please arrange follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
